   740	
   741	All four positive controls are polynomial automorphisms.  Put `u=f,v=g` and,
   742	on `v=c_2`, write the inverse as `(x,y)=(X(u),Y(u))`.  Differentiating the
   743	inverse and using `J=[f,g]` gives
   744	
   745	```text
   746	       g_y(X(u),Y(u))=J X'(u),       J dx/g_y=du.              (5.1)
   747	```
   748	
   749	Thus the natural time value is exactly `u_i=f(x,tau_i)`, with zero integration
   750	constant.  Also `1/g_y=J^-1 du_i/dx`; the derivative of a Puiseux series has no
   751	`x^-1` coefficient, because the only putative source is the derivative of an
   752	`x^0` term.  NO-RESIDUE therefore holds branchwise.  Uniqueness of the
   753	degree-`<n` interpolant recovers `f` exactly.
