   218	## Packing and Exactness
   219	
   220	For a selected orbit type, the packet is
   221	
   222	```text
   223	weight w = |O| V_2
   224	value  c = |O| V_2 q,     q = (1-delta_1) d e/(d+e).
   225	```
   226	
   227	The shared parent can only supply the degree available in its `p(pi)`. For
   228	`s=3`, the only split below the top major child is `D_2 -> D_1`, so
   229	`j=2`, `r=3`, and the parent polynomial has
   230	
   231	```text
   232	Q = V_3 d_2/d_3.
   233	```
   234	
   235	The campaign's normalized top-major pool is
   236	
   237	```text
   238	u = V_s K/d_s.
   239	```
   240	
   241	At `s=3`, `V_s=V_3`, `K=d_2`, and `d_s=d_3`, hence algebraically
   242	
   243	```text
   244	Q = V_3 d_2/d_3 = V_s K/d_s = u.
   245	```
   246	
   247	The script's control confirms this on all 305 `s=3` V-assignments, but the
   248	algebra is enough. Because there is only one parent `D_2`, there is at most
   249	one zero-centred `pi` factor. Nonzero `(10)` packets may repeat subject to
   250	degree budget; zero `(11)` packets are 0-1. This is exactly the script's Z01
   251	model at `s=3`.
   252	
   253	For `s>3`, the flat condition `sum |O_k| V_2^{(k)} <= u` is necessary but does
   254	not reconstruct the nested choices of parent factors at every level
   255	`j=s-1,...,2`. It is therefore a relaxation: if the relaxed knapsack has no
   256	integral packet, the real nested packing has none; if it has one, that may be
   257	a false survivor.
   258	
