   154	### 5.2 The charged extra control: two distinct local orbits
   155	
   195	Write `1/D_i = ρ_i x^{-1} + (exponents ≠ -1)`. A Puiseux primitive of `c/D_i` exists in `K` iff `ρ_i=0`. In `z=t^{1/R}`, `dx=-R z^{-R-1} dz`, so the `z^{-1} dz` term in `W_i dx` is produced by `[z^R]W_i`. That is `NO-RESIDUE`. Galois conjugate branches have the same residue: `h` independent scalar equations, one per orbit.
