+# The \(A_2=6\) ray: fixed \(N=6\), first global moment pages, and the non-proper Schur interface
+
+Date: 2026-09-03  
+Lane: `a2six-ray-moment-sol56-20260903`  
+Status: **PROVED-HERE arithmetic and conditional linear algebra; UNREVIEWED witness geometry; full geometric interpolation OPEN**
+
+## Executive verdict
+
+The replacement ray is correct as an unbounded ray of the implemented numerical census.  For every integer \(t\geq 0\), put
+
+\[
+ P=7t+6,
+ \qquad (n,m)= (9P,6P),
+ \qquad M=(-6P,4P,9P-2),
+ \qquad (V_2,V_3)=(1,6t+5).
+\]
+
+Then
+
+\[
+ (\delta _3,\delta _2,\delta _1)=(-1,1/6,7/12),\qquad
+ (A_2,A_1)=(6,2),\qquad q=1/2,
+\]
+
+and the unique \(s=3\) packing problem admits copies of a six-disc nonzero
+orbit.  Two copies have \(k=12\) and \(N=6\) for every \(t\).  The exact
+census rows at \(D=n=54,117,180,243\) were re-emitted, and the \(D=117\)
+member is exactly the live row in `branch-orbits-v2`.
+
+The global-rank request has a decisive information boundary.  The charged
+data determine the two proper six-disc packets and aggregate root counts, but
+do **not** determine the rooted contact tree, Galois action, tame support, or
+coefficient sharing of the non-proper roots.  Those data are part of the
+minimal input required by `globalinterp.py`.  The frozen driver accordingly
+refuses the bare \(D=54\) skeleton:
+
+```text
+ERROR: decorated input must contain n=54 branches, got 0
+```
+
+It would be false to call any matrix manufactured from an arbitrary completion
+“the” associated-graded matrix of this ray.  I therefore emitted two explicitly
+conditional direct-moment models for two declared rational witness projections:
+
+1. a raw-leaf confluent model with three channels per rigid cubic star;
+2. a rigid-star macro model with one normalized channel per bottom disc.
+
+For \(k=12\), the homogeneous raw-leaf proper cokernel is
+
+\[
+ 0,2,23,44
+\]
+
+at \(t=0,1,2,3\), and after the separate monic row it is
+
+\[
+ 0,3,24,45.
+\]
+
+Thus the bottom-only defect grows linearly once \(t\geq1\).  In the declared
+witness, the residual block inside the major \(D_2\) repairs all of this raw
+defect.  In the macro model, the residual block leaves a cokernel of size
+\(3t+2\) on the homogeneous page (\(3t+3\) with monicity), and the top-minor
+block repairs the remainder.  These repairs are exact for the witness matrices,
+not theorems about a Keller realization.
+
+There is an exact stable bottom-only affine functional.  If \(K=n-m=3P\),
+\(p=3k\), and
+
+\[
+ G_{\rm bot}(Y)=\prod_{i\in\mathrm{bottom}}(Y-\tau_i),
+\]
+
+then, whenever \(K>p\),
+
+\[
+ \Lambda_{t,k}(Y)=Y^{K-1-p}G_{\rm bot}(Y)
+\]
+
+annihilates all bottom columns and pairs to \(1\) with the monic target.  Its
+exponent is \(21t-19\) for \(k=12\) and \(21t-1\) for \(k=6\).  But on a
+non-proper column \(\eta\) it evaluates as
+
+\[
+ \Lambda_{t,k}(\eta)/D_\eta,
+\]
+
+which is generically nonzero.  The witness computations realize precisely
+that repair.  Hence the valuated rank defect is a stable invariant of the
+**bottom restriction**, not yet a cofinal invariant of the full global system.
+The missing/counterexample interface is the weighted Schur map
+
+\[
+ S_t:\operatorname{gr}U_{\rm np}\longrightarrow
+ \operatorname{coker}(\operatorname{gr}A_{{\rm bot},t}).
+\]
+
+The two-disc-orbit request also needs a custody correction.  Two six-disc
+orbits are indeed present and have identical lower data.  They do not, by
+Galois descent alone, give only two integration constants: the three roots of
+the rigid star split each disc packet into one length-six branch orbit and one
+length-twelve branch orbit.  The honest proper count is four constants.  The
+requested two constants \(C_A,C_B\) arise only after imposing two additional
+star-sharing equalities, one inside each disc packet.
+
+No geometric realization, full `POLY`, full `NO-RESIDUE`, or cofinal
+obstruction is claimed.  No exit-price assertion is made.
