+and the exact orbit-admissible set is
+
+\[
+ N_{\rm orb}=\{3,6,9,\ldots,3(3t+2)\}.
+\]
+
+Taking \(r=2\) yields \(k=12,N=6\) for every \(t\geq0\).  This proves the
+fixed-\(N\) numerical claim.  It does not prove attainment by a polynomial
+Jacobian pair.
+
