+Calling the last column one “minor disc” would conflate place and count.  The
+residual roots share the major \(D_2\) ancestor with the proper packet; the
+top-minor roots do not.  This changes first-separation factors in every
+\(D_i\), the Galois-orbit count, integration constants, and the Schur map.
