+## 6. The \(k=6,N=3\) single-orbit control
+
+The orbit law permits one six-disc packet, hence \(k=6,N=3\).  It lies below
+the campaign's \(N\geq6\) frontier and is a negative-control geometry, not a
+partial orbit.  It contains 18 proper roots.  The residual count inside the
+major \(D_2\) is now \(54t+27\), the top count remains \(9t+9\), and total
+non-proper count is \(63t+36\).
+
+On the homogeneous page:
+
+| \(t\) | \(D\) | equations | raw proper columns/rank/coker | macro proper columns/rank/coker |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 54 | 17 | 18 / 17 / 0 | 6 / 6 / 11 |
+| 1 | 117 | 38 | 18 / 18 / 20 | 6 / 6 / 32 |
+| 2 | 180 | 59 | 18 / 18 / 41 | 6 / 6 / 53 |
+| 3 | 243 | 80 | 18 / 18 / 62 | 6 / 6 / 74 |
+
+With monicity, the raw proper cokernels are \(0,21,42,63\), while the macro
+cokernels are \(12,33,54,75\).  In the same rational witness, the raw residual
+block again repairs full row rank.  The macro residual block leaves
+\(3t+2\) homogeneous or \(3t+3\) affine dimensions, and the top block repairs
+them.
+
+The control therefore behaves as expected: halving the proper packet makes the
+bottom deficit larger, but it does not protect that deficit from a sufficiently
