+## 6. The \(k=6,N=3\) single-orbit control
+
+The orbit law permits one six-disc packet, hence \(k=6,N=3\).  It lies below
+the campaign's \(N\geq6\) frontier and is a negative-control geometry, not a
+partial orbit.  It contains 18 proper roots.  The residual count inside the
+major \(D_2\) is now \(54t+27\), the top count remains \(9t+9\), and total
+non-proper count is \(63t+36\).
